---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/RealestateLayout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="GTA Real Estate Market Update: May 2026 | Cory Wong, Real Estate Agent"
  description="Monthly GTA real estate market update for May 2026. Sales trends, inventory data, pricing analysis, and what it means for buyers and sellers in Toronto, Markham, and Richmond Hill."
  canonicalPath="/market-updates"
>
  <!-- Page Hero -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="page-hero__title">GTA Market Updates</h1>
      <p class="page-hero__subtitle">
        Regular insights on real estate trends across the Greater Toronto Area, with a focus
        on Toronto, Markham, and Richmond Hill.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Article -->
  <article class="article">
    <div class="container content-narrow">
      <header class="article__header">
        <h2 class="article__title">GTA Real Estate Market Update: May 2026</h2>
        <p class="article__byline">By Cory Wong, Real Estate Agent</p>
      </header>

      <div class="article__intro">
        <p>
          The spring market has delivered mixed signals. Sales activity picked up from winter
          lows but remains below the 10-year average. Inventory continued to grow, and buyers
          have more leverage than they've had in recent years. Here's what the data is telling us.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Price Trends -->
      <section class="article__section">
        <h3 class="article__section-title">Price Trends</h3>
        <p>
          GTA-wide, average sale prices held roughly flat month-over-month. The picture varies
          significantly by area and property type:
        </p>
        <ul class="article__list">
          <li>
            <strong>Markham and Richmond Hill</strong> have remained resilient for detached
            homes, with prices holding steady or seeing modest gains as families continue to
            prioritize strong school districts and suburban space.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Toronto condos</strong> have softened. Downtown units in particular are
            seeing price reductions, driven by elevated inventory and competition from new
            construction completions entering the resale market.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Inventory and Days on Market -->
      <section class="article__section">
        <h3 class="article__section-title">Inventory and Days on Market</h3>
        <p>
          Active listings are up approximately 25% year-over-year across the GTA. Months of
          inventory have climbed above 3 for detached homes and above 4 for condos &mdash;
          levels that favour buyers or at minimum create a more balanced market.
        </p>
        <p>
          Average days on market sit at around 18 days, though well-priced properties in
          desirable areas continue to sell faster.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- What This Means for Buyers -->
      <section class="article__section">
        <h3 class="article__section-title">What This Means for Buyers</h3>
        <p>
          Buyers have more time and more options than they've had in years. The urgency that
          characterized 2021 and 2022 is largely absent, and conditions allow for more
          thorough due diligence and measured decision-making.
        </p>
        <p>
          That said, well-priced homes in sought-after neighbourhoods are still drawing multiple
          offers. The market rewards preparation: buyers who have financing in order and know
          their target areas are best positioned to move quickly when the right property appears.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- What This Means for Sellers -->
      <section class="article__section">
        <h3 class="article__section-title">What This Means for Sellers</h3>
        <p>
          Pricing accurately matters more now than it has in years. Overpriced listings sit,
          accumulate days on market, and often end up selling for less than they would have with
          a realistic initial price. The sellers seeing the best results are those who price
          competitively from day one and present their homes well.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Looking Ahead -->
      <section class="article__section">
        <h3 class="article__section-title">Looking Ahead</h3>
        <p>
          The Bank of Canada's rate path will continue to shape market sentiment. Upcoming
          inflation data and employment numbers will influence whether further rate adjustments
          are on the table. Any meaningful rate movement would likely accelerate buyer activity,
          particularly in the condo segment where affordability pressures are most acute.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <div class="article__cta">
        <a href="/contact" class="cta cta--primary">Book a Consultation</a>
      </div>

      <!-- Disclaimer -->
      <div class="article__disclaimer">
        <p>
          The information in this report is based on publicly available data from the Toronto
          Regional Real Estate Board and other sources. It is intended for general informational
          purposes only and should not be relied upon as a substitute for professional advice
          specific to your situation. Market conditions change rapidly. Speak with Cory for a
          current assessment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- Newsletter -->
  <section class="newsletter">
    <div class="container content-narrow">
      <h2 class="newsletter__heading">Stay Informed</h2>
      <p class="newsletter__text">
        Get monthly market data, neighbourhood insights, and practical advice for buyers
        and sellers across the Greater Toronto Area.
      </p>
      <form id="newsletter-form" class="newsletter__form" novalidate>
        <input
          type="email"
          id="newsletter-email"
          name="email"
          placeholder="you@example.com"
          required
          autocomplete="email"
          class="newsletter__input"
        />
        <button type="submit" class="cta cta--primary newsletter__btn">Subscribe</button>
      </form>
      <p id="newsletter-form-status" class="form-status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<script>
  const newsletterForm = document.getElementById('newsletter-form') as HTMLFormElement | null;
  const newsletterStatus = document.getElementById('newsletter-form-status');

  if (newsletterForm && newsletterStatus) {
    newsletterForm.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      newsletterStatus.textContent = '';
      newsletterStatus.className = 'form-status';

      const formData = new FormData(newsletterForm);
      const payload = {
        type: 'newsletter',
        email: formData.get('email'),
      };

      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/lead', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload),
        });

        if (res.ok) {
          newsletterStatus.textContent = 'You\'re subscribed! Watch your inbox for the next report.';
          newsletterStatus.classList.add('form-status--success');
          newsletterForm.reset();
        } else {
          throw new Error('Request failed');
        }
      } catch {
        newsletterStatus.textContent = 'Something went wrong. Please try again.';
        newsletterStatus.classList.add('form-status--error');
      }
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  .content-narrow {
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  /* Page Hero */
  .page-hero {
    padding: var(--space-2xl) 0 var(--space-xl);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .page-hero__title {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .page-hero__subtitle {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  /* Article */
  .article {
    padding: 0 0 var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .article__header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .article__title {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .article__byline {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .article__intro {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .article__intro p {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .article__section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .article__section-title {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .article__section p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .article__section p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .article__list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  .article__list li {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
    position: relative;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .article__list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.625rem;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .article__list li:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* CTA */
  .article__cta {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-xl);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .cta {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background-color 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .cta--primary {
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .cta--primary:hover {
    background: var(--color-accent-hover);
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  /* Disclaimer */
  .article__disclaimer {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .article__disclaimer p {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* Newsletter */
  .newsletter {
    padding: var(--space-2xl) 0;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: #ffffff;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .newsletter__heading {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .newsletter__text {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    opacity: 0.9;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .newsletter__form {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    max-width: 28rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .newsletter__input {
    flex: 1;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    padding: 0.625rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.3);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .newsletter__input::placeholder {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
  }

  .newsletter__input:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: #ffffff;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25);
  }

  .newsletter__btn {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    border: 1px solid #ffffff;
    background: #ffffff;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .newsletter__btn:hover {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .form-status {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    min-height: 1.25rem;
  }

  .newsletter .form-status--success {
    color: #ffffff;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  .newsletter .form-status--error {
    color: #fecaca;
  }

  /* Responsive */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .newsletter__form {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
</style>
